.TH "SKARN-FLEET" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.33.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-fleet \- Fold drops into the org aggregate; render the executive
readout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBfleet\fR \fIaggregate|readout\fR \fIpath\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fold a directory of per\-machine drop artifacts into the fleet aggregate that
serve \-\-fleet renders (aggregate), or render the leadership readout from one
or two aggregates (readout). Both are Enterprise: without a covering license
they refuse with exit 5 before reading any file, and with no usable license at
all they exit 7; \-\-help stays ungated.
.PP
The consuming half of the fleet kit, inside the binary. fleet aggregate reads
the drop artifacts under <dropdir> (flat <dropdir>/*.json, or one
<dropdir>/<identity>/ subdirectory per machine named the way check \-\-drop
names it), validates every one of them against the drop schema and against the
scope it declares, refuses the run outright when any drop is rejected (naming
the drop and the reason on stderr, writing nothing, exit 1), and writes
aggregate schema version 4 atomically to \-o. Given \-\-roster it also refuses
a drop from a machine the roster does not name or a project the roster does
not permit that machine, accepts an unscoped drop only from a machine the
roster marks allowUnscoped, and records coverage: how many machines were
expected, how many reported, and which did not. fleet readout renders the
Markdown readout a leadership audience reads from one aggregate, or from two
when \-\-prior names the previous period's aggregate, which is what turns
positions into movements; \-\-json emits the underlying comparison object.
Both subcommands are Enterprise: without a covering license they refuse with
exit 5 before reading any file, and with no usable license at all they exit 7
like check; \-\-help is ungated. The aggregate carries only what the drops
carry, and the readout prints machine identities, counts and months, never a
finding, a rule id, a project name or a secret preview.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR
With aggregate: the aggregate file to write, required; it is written
atomically through a temporary file in the same directory, so a refused run
leaves no partial aggregate behind. With readout: write the rendered readout
there instead of standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-roster\fR \fIfile\fR
With aggregate: the org\-controlled roster of the machines expected to report
and the projects each may report on. A drop from a machine the roster does not
name is refused; a drop that resolved a project the roster does not permit
that machine is refused naming both; an unscoped drop is accepted only from a
machine the roster marks allowUnscoped; and the aggregate gains a coverage
block naming every rostered machine that sent nothing. Without it the machine
set is discovered from the drops and a machine that never reported is
invisible.
.TP
\fB\-\-prior\fR \fIaggregate\fR
With readout: the previous period's aggregate. The readout then reports
movements against it; omitted, it states that this is the baseline
measurement. The prior must be for the same organization and older than the
current aggregate.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
With readout: emit the underlying comparison object (coverage, fleet totals,
per\-machine movement, the ranked risk list) instead of Markdown; without
\-\-prior the movement fields are null.
